# Close Encounter's additional cost, "choose a creature you control or a warped creature card you own in exile", can't be paid
# with nothing to choose (CR 601.2h), so the attempted cast rolls back though its mana is there (CR 733.1). On turn 3 Bot1 controls no creature.
# Its own Ornithopter and Memnite are in exile but not warped (CR 702.185b): Oblivion Ring's triggered ability exiled the one,
# Bot2's Swords to Plowshares the other. Bot2's Timeline Culler is a warped creature card in exile, but Bot2 owns it. And
# Bot2's Memnite is a creature Bot1 doesn't control.

